# topo-fanout-fanin-declared-order — A fans out to B and to C; neither B nor C
# pipes to the other; both fan in to D before D egresses. Unlike pipe-fanout
# (where a direct A -> C edge forces a unique topological order), B and C are
# mutually incomparable here: the pipe relation admits both A,B,C,D and
# A,C,B,D as valid topological orders (SPEC §7.2, §7.4). B is declared before
# C, so the declaration-order tie-break (SPEC §7.4) fixes the log as A, B, C, D.
# a holds no grant at C, so C is refused (checked at every gate, §5.1/§7.1);
# D's effective verdict is the join of its own auto, B's auto, and C's
# refused -> refused, exercising restrictions composing over a second
# fan-out/fan-in topology distinct from pipe-fanout's.
actor a
gate  A grant a
gate  B grant a
gate  C
gate  D grant a
cord a -> A
cord A -> B
cord A -> C
cord B -> D
cord C -> D
cord D -> master
